% Synthetic proposals for the California homeowners guide (california.le):
% one that passes, one that fails or is referred for each topic of the
% guide's eligibility pages, the brush table row by row where it matters,
% and borderline cases (a fact left out, the empty cell of the brush table,
% a judgment nobody has made yet). Each scenario's comment says what it
% tests. The proposals are invented: they test that the guidelines were
% captured faithfully, not how the insurer decides.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program is an example of Logical English. It is provided
% "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including any
% warranty that it is accurate, complete, up to date or fit for a particular
% purpose. It is not an official reading of the underwriting guidelines it
% cites, it is not an underwriting decision of any insurer, and it is not
% legal or insurance advice. Its answers may be wrong: do not rely on them
% for a real application; consult the insurer and a licensed agent. Its
% authors accept no liability for any loss or damage arising from its use.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base california cases includes these resources:
    california.

the knowledge base california cases includes:

query decision is:
    the decision on which proposal is which action.

query ineligible is:
    which proposal is ineligible under which guideline.

query referred is:
    which proposal must be referred to underwriting under which guideline.

query brush is:
    the brush decision for which dwelling is which action.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        application 201 is eligible.

% A thirty-year-old wood-frame house, composition roof eight years old,
% central heating, 200 amps, copper plumbing, protection class 3, low wildfire
% scores. Nothing in the guide stops it.
scenario clean is:
    application 201 is for the Elm Drive house.
    application 201 is dated 2026-09-01.
    the policy form of application 201 is homeowners.
    the Elm Drive house was previously insured, according to the applicant.
    the dwelling limit of application 201 is 650000, according to the applicant.
    the personal property limit of application 201 is 325000, according to the applicant.
    the construction of the Elm Drive house is wood frame, according to the applicant.
    the age of the Elm Drive house is 30 years, according to the applicant.
    the roof of the Elm Drive house is made of composition shingle, according to the applicant.
    the roof of the Elm Drive house is 8 years old, according to the applicant.
    the primary heat source of the Elm Drive house is central heating, according to the applicant.
    the electrical service of the Elm Drive house is 200 amps, according to the applicant.
    the plumbing of the Elm Drive house is copper, according to the applicant.
    the occupancy of the Elm Drive house is owner occupied, according to the applicant.
    the protection class of the Elm Drive house is 3, as stated in the protection class report.
    the Elm Drive house is 2 miles from a fire department, as stated in the protection class report.
    the fireline score of the Elm Drive house is 0, as stated in the wildfire report.
    the wildfire score of the Elm Drive house is 1.2, as stated in the wildfire report.
    decision expects answers ["the decision on application 201 is accept"].
    ineligible expects answers [].
    referred expects answers [].
    brush expects answers ["the brush decision for the Elm Drive house is accept"].

